The '''twelfth series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' began airing on 21 September 2021.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-58544950 |title=Great British Baking Show 2021 contestants revealed |work=BBC |date=14 September 2021 }}</ref> It is presented by [[Noel Fielding]] and [[Matt Lucas]], and judged by returning judges [[Paul Hollywood]] and [[Prue Leith]]. The bakers were announced on 14 September 2021.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|date=2021-09-13|title=Meet the contestants for the 12th series of The Great British Bake Off|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/bake-off-contestants-who-2021-b1919307.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/bake-off-contestants-who-2021-b1919307.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live|access-date=2021-09-13|website=The Independent|language=en}}</ref>

The series was won by [[Giuseppe Dell'Anno]], with Chigs Parmar and Crystelle Pereira finishing as the runners-up. Dell'Anno is the first Italian winner of the programme.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/live/2021/nov/23/the-great-british-bake-off-2021-final-live|title=The Great British Bake Off 2021: final – as it happened|date=23 November 2021|work=Guardian|accessdate=24 November 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-59390446|title=The Great British Bake Off crowns its 2021 winner|date=23 November 2021|work=BBC|accessdate=24 November 2021}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Bennett |first=Paige |title=First vegan baker on the 'Great British Baking Show' shares what it was really like on the series |url=https://www.insider.com/bake-off-vegan-baker-what-show-judges-like-freya-cox-interview-2022 |access-date=2022-09-27 |website=Insider |language=en-US}}</ref>

