== Ratings ==
''Bake Off'' launched with 5.7 million viewers and a 30.8% share—its lowest overnight rating since its move to Channel 4 in 2017—down 1.3 million in 2020.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a37687829/great-british-bake-off-2021-launch-show-ratings/ |title=Great British Bake Off suffers lowest launch show ratings since Channel 4 move |first=Sam|last= Warner|date= 22 September 2021|work=Digital Spy}}</ref>  However, it was the show's biggest ever launch episode on Channel 4 in terms of younger viewers, securing 61.9% of all young viewers watching TV at the time of broadcast.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/C4Press/status/1440609899201773572 |title=Delicious #GBBO return last night is highest rating @Channel4 commission so far this year |date= 22 September 2021|work=Channel 4 Press}}</ref>{{primary source inline|date=August 2024}}

